      "content": "okay, that makes sense technically. so it's really just about isolating those fields into their own tables so they aren't hanging off the wrong keys.\n\ni guess i'm just still stuck on the \"annoyance\" part. you mentioned it's like they're hiding or just lurking around—does that actually reflect how these dependencies behave in a real-world system? like, is there a way they can \"infest\" a system or cause some kind of systemic chaos if you don't catch them early enough?",
      "source": "evaluator"
