      "content": "Yes, the \"infestation\" is a perfect description of the systemic chaos! When you have these transitive dependencies, it's not just a minor annoyance; it leads to data anomalies, which are the true source of database headaches. If you have to update a department name, and that name is stored redundantly across fifty different employee records, you have to update all fifty—if you miss even one, you have an inconsistency, which is a data nightmare. This is the real-world consequence of letting those structural flaws linger.",
